51	da35cbec-908f-4d38-8b36-43bca3d3bcd8	5193e750-4393-4f52-bd3b-9cfa5a9f5587	As for your lessons, now, I think they're BRILLIANT. I wish my personal library was unpacked because I would take a picture for you. I have what seems like every title imaginable, from historical fiction to in-depth study books of biographies and diaries on almost every historical culture from Ancient Egyptians, Greeks, and Roman's all the way up to (my former obsession) The Tudors and beyond. I just wanted to commend you because I feel like it's all starting to become lost and you've done an incredible job of making it come alive. I look forward to following along with Kellen's documents for your class. I really just wanted to say thank you 😊	2026-02-06 04:14:01.126	teacher_portal	\N	3aa03478-c637-4066-ad20-f0f41fbba4d4	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	f	\N
52	da35cbec-908f-4d38-8b36-43bca3d3bcd8	5193e750-4393-4f52-bd3b-9cfa5a9f5587	Hahaha oh my goodness I completely understand. I took forensics and forensic anatomy for 4 semesters of high school and became completely enthralled in the macabre medical practices dating from medieval (honestly my favorite time period) up until even now! If you are interested in a funny, yet very respectful book, I recommend Mary Roach's "STIFF". I am now 37 and I read it at least once a year. She has a way of being hilarious with an impressive amount of reverence for the deceased. "What the Corpse Revealed" is more just forensics and applying it to solving cases, but it is also a wonderful read.	2026-02-06 04:07:49.558	teacher_portal	\N	f27e825a-0e5b-45bb-8125-d3a5c373c437	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	f	\N
