527	24723696-63bd-4947-aab0-7fafd0978f39	6c184edb-5677-4864-975b-0693b2911d41	Hello Alison!\n\nI hope you and your family have been doing well! I really enjoyed working with your boys during our Finance 101 lessons a few weeks ago and wanted to follow up with some options for continuing in May.\n\nUpcoming Lesson Topics\nHere’s what we’d be diving into next:\n\n1. Macroeconomics (Next Lesson)\n\t• What the economy is and how it works as a whole\n\t• How GDP connects to the economy\n\t• Why the U.S. has one of the strongest economies\n\t• How the economy grows over time\nAs before, this lesson is broken down with discussion, interactive activities, and games to keep it engaging and easy to understand.\n\n2. Recessions & Economic Events (Following Lesson)\n\t• What a recession is and when the U.S. has experienced one\n\t• How the 1970s Oil Crisis affected prices and daily life\n\t• How COVID-19 impacted jobs, money, and the economy\n\t• What unemployment means and how it’s measured\n\t• Understanding national debt and the current U.S. situation\n\nScheduling Options (ET & PT)\nI kept your PT schedule in mind, assuming the boys are still in school during the day:\n\t• Wed, April 29 – 8:00 pm ET (5:00 pm PT) \n\t• Thurs, April 30 – 6:00 pm ET (3:00 pm PT) or 7:00 pm ET (4:00 pm PT) \n\t• Fri, May 1 – 8:00 pm ET (5:00 pm PT) \n\t• Mon, May 4 – 7:00 pm ET (4:00 pm PT) \n\t• Wed, May 6 – 8:00 pm ET (5:00 pm PT) \n\t• Fri, May 8 – 8:00 pm ET (5:00 pm PT) \n\t• Mon, May 11 – 7:00 pm ET (4:00 pm PT) \n\t• Wed, May 13 – 6:00 pm ET (3:00 pm PT) or 8:00 pm ET (5:00 pm PT) \n\t• Thurs, May 14 – 7:00 pm ET (4:00 pm PT) or 8:00 pm ET (5:00 pm PT) \n\t• Fri, May 15 – 8:00 pm ET (5:00 pm PT) \n\t• Mon, May 18 – 7:00 pm ET (4:00 pm PT) \n\t• Wed, May 20 – 6:00 pm ET (3:00 pm PT) or 8:00 pm ET (5:00 pm PT) \n\t• Thurs, May 21 – 7:00 pm ET (4:00 pm PT) \n\t• Fri, May 22 – 8:00 pm ET (5:00 pm PT) \n\t• Mon, May 25 – 7:00 pm ET (4:00 pm PT) \n\t• Wed, May 27 – 6:00 pm ET (3:00 pm PT) or 8