528	24723696-63bd-4947-aab0-7fafd0978f39	6c184edb-5677-4864-975b-0693b2911d41	Sharing a quick update on today’s second lesson with your boys—they did a great job!\n\nWe explored how the Federal Reserve controls the money supply and talked about why excessive money printing can lead to inflation. We connected this to real life by discussing how prices increased during COVID and how we’ve all experienced inflation firsthand. The boys also participated in a “money detective” activity where they investigated how the cost of everyday items has changed over the past 15 years.\n\nOverall, it was another really strong session. Kyle and Aiden were noticeably more engaged this time, and all three boys participated thoughtfully throughout. In our second Kahoot game, they were focused and competitive in a great way—Kyle came in first, Micah second, and Aiden third.\n\nI’d love to continue building on this momentum with more lessons in the coming weeks as schedules allow, so let’s definitely stay in touch!	2026-03-30 18:10:21.302	teacher_portal	\N	830705ac-efde-4a36-ab82-8a40c6c2d88d	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	f	\N
