533	24723696-63bd-4947-aab0-7fafd0978f39	6c184edb-5677-4864-975b-0693b2911d41	Quick update --We covered Topic 1: The Story of Money just now. The boys learned what finance means, why it’s important to start learning it early, how money solves the bartering problem, and how it has evolved from coins to paper money to digital currency. We also talked about the flow of money and how it never “sleeps”—it’s always moving between people and businesses.\n\nI really enjoyed seeing all three of them on camera—they were engaged throughout the lesson. Micah stood out with his curiosity and thoughtful questions, and he even earned first place in our Kahoot game! Kyle was a bit reserved at first, but once I let him know I’d be calling on him more, he really started to participate. Aiden and Kyle definitely have fun, playful energy and enjoy making each other laugh—I did notice that they can sometimes distract one another, but separating them into different rooms is already making a positive difference.\n\nDuring our game, I wasn’t always sure if Kyle and Aiden were choosing some answers just for fun or not trying their best, but I’m still getting to know their personalities. They both bring a lot of energy to the group, which I love, and I’ll continue working to channel that into focused participation while keeping things fun.\n\nI’m really looking forward to our next lesson coming up shortly in a few minutes on Topic 2: Inflation!	2026-03-30 17:00:26.982	teacher_portal	\N	cc4aadb5-ddec-4b7b-8b41-f2f54218b508	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	f	\N
