969	f4888850-c3f9-4244-ab83-ac10d7a2c42f	0e7c64cc-5552-40bf-8237-7785cd04de65	Hi K. Freeman,\n\nThank you so much for reaching out — I’m glad to hear you’re considering our Week in News class for your children!\n\nHere’s a quick overview of the format and what to expect:\n\n1. Each session begins with a short, engaging presentation of age-appropriate current events. These are carefully chosen to be informative but never overwhelming or intense. Each week, we explore a fresh set of unbiased news articles covering science, culture, global events, and discoveries. Together, we break them down by looking at facts vs. opinions, identifying bias, and sparking thoughtful conversations.\n\n2. Learners are encouraged to share their thoughts and ask questions, & debate perspectives, but no one is ever put on the spot. If your child prefers to listen at first, that’s absolutely fine — participation can build gradually as they get more comfortable.\n\n3. Each week’s articles are shared ahead of time (optional to review), so learners can come prepared if they’d like, or simply engage during the live discussion.\n\n4. We also end every session with a fun Kahoot quiz to reinforce what we’ve learned. To answer your specific question: students are not required to debate or share from the very start. Many learners begin by simply listening and later join in when they feel ready. Also since this class is a mix of current events, discussion & debate: good part of the session also involves them hearing about the most relevant happenings around the world.\n\nI also saw your note about the duplicate message — no worries at all, these things happen! Hope this helps :)	2025-09-22 20:30:23.444	teacher_portal	\N	78811e28-135b-4f5b-b21d-31a55a74462b	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	f	\N
